# Build context for packages/domain-api/Dockerfile and packages/web/Dockerfile (built
# from the repo root as context). This is not just .gitignore: it also drops
# version-controlled files (docs, CI workflows, agent/policy tooling) that are legitimately
# committed but that no image build ever COPYs, to keep the context small and to stop an
# unrelated doc/CI edit from being sent to the daemon on every build.

# Dependencies (reinstalled fresh inside each build stage)
node_modules/

# Build outputs (regenerated inside the image; a stray root dist/ has existed locally from
# ad hoc `tsc` runs outside Docker and must never be picked up as if it were build output)
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/

# VCS / local tool state
.git/
.omc/
.openforge/

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Environment / secrets — never bake these into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Logs / caches / temp
*.log
logs/
.cache/
tmp/
temp/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Committed content no Dockerfile COPYs: docs, agent/skill instructions, CI, non-container
# verification tooling, and repo-hygiene files. Anchored to the repo root (leading slash)
# so these don't shadow same-named directories inside packages/*, e.g.
# packages/domain-api/tests/ (needed for that package's own typecheck) and
# packages/policy-compiler/tests/ are NOT excluded by the root-level /tests/ below.
/.agents/
/.github/
/docs/
/research/
/templates/
/scripts/
/tests/
/*.md
/LICENSE
